        "acceptedPr": null,
        "calls": 2,
        "title": "Server can hide the plan upgrade button via new wire flag",
        "summary": "The shared wire type for the Freebucks meter in the common package now carries an optional `upgradeHidden` flag. When the server sets it to true, clients must suppress the upgrade button, including the next plan offer for subscribers, because the account's current tier pools cover its usage. The flag overrides the existing `upgrade` field, which remains the mechanism for displaying an upgrade prompt when present. This allows full-access accounts on lower tiers to skip the upsell without the client making its own decision about entitlements.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "The diff adds a new optional boolean field `upgradeHidden` to the `FreebuffFreebucksInfo` interface in `common/src/types/freebuff-session.ts`, with a JSDoc comment explaining that it is the server's verdict to hide the upgrade button for full access tiers 1 and 2.",
        "userVisible": true,
        "confidence": "medium",
        "unknowns": "The diff defines the wire contract but does not show the specific client logic changes that consume this flag to hide the UI elements.",
        "at": "2026-10-23T00:16:15.719Z",
        "cf": "0582b43ceafe"
