        "calls": 2,
        "title": "Compaction reserves user memory, BYOK fixes Azure OpenAI",
        "summary": "The agent runtime compaction pass now reserves a dedicated budget, `USER_MEMORY_TOKENS` (24000 tokens), for the user's earlier requests and the newest to-do list, shortening oversized requests instead of dropping them. This change in `packages/agent-runtime/src/compact-history.ts` ensures that key context survives mechanical compaction rather than being evicted by older tool history. Simultaneously, `sdk/src/impl/byok-request.ts` adds support for Azure OpenAI reasoning models by converting `max_tokens` to `max_completion_tokens` and removing the `stop` field when the endpoint matches `AZURE_OPENAI_HOST` and the model is identified by `isOpenAIReasoningModel`.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "In `packages/agent-runtime/src/compact-history.ts`, the `compactRequestHistory` function now reserves `USER_MEMORY_TOKENS` (24000) for user requests and the newest to-do list; in `sdk/src/impl/byok-request.ts`, the `byokRequestTransform` function detects Azure OpenAI hosts using `isOpenAIReasoningModel` to replace `max_tokens` with `max_completion_tokens`.",
